# Encoded H_L ⊗ H_S on a Knill C4 [[4,2,2]] block (Fig 12 top of
# quant-ph/0410199). Transversal physical H on all 4 qubits, then relabel
# the middle two output qubits to undo the L↔S swap that transversal H induces
# with Knill's convention.
# The gadget's output support carries the permutation instead of a physical
# SWAP, whose correlated two-qubit faults can cause undetected logical errors.
#
# Action on Knill C4 logicals (X_L = X_0 X_1, X_S = X_1 X_3,
# Z_L = Z_0 Z_2, Z_S = Z_2 Z_3):
#   X_L → Z_L   (X_0 X_1 →(H) Z_0 Z_1 →(relabel 1 2) Z_0 Z_2 = Z_L)
#   X_S → Z_S   (X_1 X_3 →(H) Z_1 Z_3 →(relabel 1 2) Z_2 Z_3 = Z_S)
#   Z_L → X_L   (Z_0 Z_2 →(H) X_0 X_2 →(relabel 1 2) X_0 X_1 = X_L)
#   Z_S → X_S   (Z_2 Z_3 →(H) X_2 X_3 →(relabel 1 2) X_1 X_3 = X_S)

H 0 1 2 3
